Thought: Test a simple robust baseline: mean over full pool (trend-dominated, moderate seasonality).  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full","rationale":"baseline mean"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and correlation groups suggest combining weighted by inverse error across the full pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error","rationale":"inverse_error weighting over full pool"}

Thought: Try a robust DBA combination to see if it beats weighted inverse_error on this trend-dominated series.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: The series has unstable ranking and strong trend; testing a per‑horizon weighted top‑k may capture horizon‑specific strengths.  
Action: select_top_k  
Action Input: {"k":7,"metric":"smape"}

Thought: The series is trend dominated with unstable rankings; a robust trimmed‑mean on a small, highly correlated pool may reduce variance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool4","trim_pct":0.2,"rationale":"trimmed mean on stable top‑7 to dampen outliers"}

Thought: Ranking is unstable and errors are highly correlated; a per‑horizon best‑model weighting may capture horizon‑specific strengths.  
Action: weights_best_per_horizon  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","metric":"rmse"}

Thought: test a different weighting strategy (softmax_neg_error) to see if a probabilistic weighting outperforms inverse_error on this trend‑dominated series with unstable rankings.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: test a per‑horizon weighted combination using the best‑per‑horizon handle (w3) to capture horizon‑specific strengths, a different strategy type than previous weighted or mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w3","rationale":"per‑horizon best weights"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and a robust median over the full pool may outperform DBA by reducing influence of outliers.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full","rationale":"robust median over all models"}

Thought: The series has unstable ranking and strong trend; a trimmed mean on a stable top‑7 pool may reduce noise while keeping trend models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool4","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: The series is trend-dominated with unstable rankings; a robust trimmed mean over all models may reduce influence of correlated errors.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: The series has unstable ranking and strong trend; a robust weighted combo with softmax_neg_error on the stable top‑7 pool might capture complementary strengths.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"softmax_neg_error","rationale":"softmax weighting on stable pool"}

Thought: test a weighted inverse_error over the stable pool4 to see if a simpler weight on fewer models improves over softmax on pool4.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"inverse_error","rationale":"inverse_error on reduced stable pool"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and the top models cluster into two groups; a softmax weighting over the full pool may better balance them than inverse_error.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error","rationale":"softmax weighting over full pool to capture complementary errors"}

Thought: The series has unstable ranking and a strong trend; a robust median over a stable subset (pool4) might reduce variance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4","rationale":"robust median on stable top‑7"}

Thought: ranking is unstable and several models form correlated groups; a per‑horizon best‑model weighting may capture changing strengths across horizons.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"best_per_horizon","rationale":"per‑horizon best‑model weighting on full pool"}

Thought: The series is trend‑dominated with unstable rankings, so a robust DBA on the stable top‑7 pool may outperform the current DBA on all models.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool4","dba_max_iter":30,"rationale":"robust DBA on stable top‑7"}

